"guide.lineupSpread":"<b>Not a confirmed mechanic.</b> This is playing experience shared in alliance chat, not something read off a game panel or a vetted guide. It is recorded because it is specific and testable, not because it is established. <ul><li>The advice is to <b>avoid putting your strongest tank and your strongest carry on the same side</b> of the formation — swap the back corners so the two flanks are balanced rather than one being loaded.</li><li>The reasoning offered: with both weakest heroes on one side, <b>that flank collapses sooner, the enemy reaches your support faster</b>, and the fight is lost earlier than the raw stats suggest.</li><li>A separate suggestion from the same conversation: against the <b>Demon King</b>, running a <b>third carry in place of a tank</b> reportedly performs better.</li></ul><p class=\"opinion-src\">Shared by <b>Shiney</b>, with the Demon King variant from <b>hellokatzchen</b> crediting <b>TheyCallMeJoe</b>. Alliance chat, 1 Aug 2026.</p>",
"guide.rcsConflict":"<b>This contradicts the duration recorded elsewhere on this page.</b> The note above the timeline says the in-game rules give a Saturday <b>12:00–16:00</b> window, a four-hour event. This Rules tab says the Scramble <b>lasts eight hours</b>, with four hours being the <i>occupation total</i> needed to win rather than the length of the event. Both readings came from in-game text, so one of them is a stale or different panel. The observed <b>Friday 12:00 start</b> for #217 is unaffected either way; it is the <b>end time that is now unverified</b>. A screenshot of the event countdown once the Scramble is live would settle it.",
"guide.lineupAmbiguity":"<b>Unresolved — “unit type” is not defined.</b> The excerpt says <i>same unit type</i> without saying whether that means <b>faction</b> (Warrior / Ranger / Warlock) or something else such as troop type or hero role. The quiz consistently says <b>faction</b> and gives the same 5-hero figure, so faction is the likely reading and is assumed here — but the two texts also describe the payoff differently: the excerpt says <b>HP, ATK and DEF</b>, the quiz says <b>damage</b>. Those may be one mechanic described loosely, or two separate ones. A screenshot of the in-game lineup or faction-bonus panel would settle both questions at once.",
"guide.epiPlanConflict":"<b>Unresolved — what actually unlocks plan slots.</b> The same guide says it two ways on one page: the plans panel says slots open <i>as you evolve</i>, while its own quick-tips list says to <b>use Shards to upgrade the Epigraph Workshop and unlock more plan slots</b>. Those are different currencies driving the same unlock. Both are recorded until a live panel settles it.",
"note.howtoPaths":"Button paths are shown as numbered chains rather than screenshots, so the page stays one small file and the steps cannot rot when an image host expires. <b>The button names are given in English</b> because no localised screenshots of these menus exist yet — per the rule used throughout this page, a game string is never guessed. Unlike a screenshot, these chains can be translated once localised menus are confirmed.",
"guide.exwWarn":"<b>Flagged as not confirmed for this game.</b> The source infographic states on its own face that it is based on information from <b>Era of Revival</b> servers and that features may change before reaching all kingdoms. It also uses a hero taxonomy — Defense / Attack / Strategy — that does not match the Warrior / Ranger / Warlock factions used everywhere else, including by the game’s own quiz. Treat everything below as unverified and possibly not applicable here.",
"guide.epiGap":"<b>Still open.</b> The fourth class name now leans Initiative rather than Warning (see table above), but the source screenshot had two overlapping UI text elements, so treat it as leaning, not settled. <b>Part 2 of the “1/2” guide has still not surfaced</b> — the third guide supplied here is a separate document, not its continuation. One guide also states that Raven Development Level “increases based on total sales”, which is unclear and is contradicted by the in-game panel showing it driven by EXP Books; that phrasing is not recorded above.",
"note.guidesTbdHow":"<b>Nothing here yet.</b> Send the guides and this fills in. Each will get its own block with the author, source link and date, the same as the event guides — and anything that contradicts a screenshot-verified fact will be flagged rather than quietly overwritten.",
"guide.titlesGap":"<b>One item still open.</b> The panel is headed “King Bonus” rather than naming a recipient, so it is not stated whether those four bonuses apply only to the King or to the whole kingdom while a King is seated. <b>The leaning is towards the King alone</b>, on the grounds that the panel uses the same avatar-name-bonus layout as the eight title panels, where the bonuses demonstrably belong to the holder. That is a structural argument, not a confirmation. <b>What would settle it:</b> a non-King player checking their own active buff list — if a King-derived bonus appears there, it is kingdom-wide. Separately, the Minister of the Inner Court resource percentages still want a second account’s screenshot to confirm they are flat title values.",
"guide.dkGap":"<b>Spawn hour still unknown.</b> A countdown of 05:19:50 was observed at 18:30 server time, putting the despawn at roughly 23:50 server — consistent with the Blight lasting until the 00:00 daily reset, and an earlier reading of 11:53:32 fits the same pattern. That is inference from two countdowns, not a confirmed schedule, and it gives the <i>end</i> rather than the start. A screenshot taken shortly after a Blight appears would settle it.",
"tools.falconExpiry":"<b>Complete them, just don’t claim them.</b> Completing and claiming are two separate actions. Any quest you leave <i>uncompleted</i> will <b>expire and be lost</b> — so keep completing as they arrive, and hold back only the claim.",
"guide.taGap":"<b>Still unknown.</b> Arena of Fate’s format, challenge count and rewards have not been captured — only its entry gate and tier structure. Neither arena’s season length is confirmed; the ten-day figure is inferred from a single countdown. And it is not established whether the top-200 and top-1,200 gates are measured per kingdom or across the pooled kingdoms.",
"guide.elixirStarNote":"<b>Transcribed from screenshots of the source sheet.</b> Figures and effects are as printed there. The star priorities on the two lowest rows (Migration Portal, Camps) are the hardest to resolve at that resolution — worth a second look if you are ranking targets by them.",
"guide.cvGap":"<b>Schedule partly confirmed.</b> A live entry screen (2 Aug 2026) showed four daily slots in the device's local time: 06:00–06:30, 13:00–13:30, 22:00–22:30 and 03:00–03:30 (next day) — irregular spacing, not evenly every 6 hours. These are genuine observed times, but converting them to server time (GMT−2) needs the device's own UTC offset, which the screenshot doesn't state, so the four Sunday server-time windows this page uses remain a working assumption pending that conversion. Also still open: exact scoring rates, what makes the Sacred Cave the top location, and whether ranking is individual or alliance-wide.",
"note.tools":"Tools built and maintained by other players. These are external links &mdash; they are not part of this page and we do not control their contents or availability.",
"tools.speedupTitle":"Speed-Up Calculator",
"tools.speedupBody":"Enter how many of each speed-up you hold and it totals the time, in minutes and in days/hours/minutes. The top block covers general-use speed-ups, the bottom block task-specific ones. Version 2 adds build-queue times and shows whether you have enough banked to cover all current projects. Make your own copy before entering anything.",
"tools.speedupCredit":"Built by <b>Corlanthis v1.0#1029</b>, posted to the Discord guide section on 29 Jul 2026.",
